==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/plʌmp/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ʌmp|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{context|intransitive|lang=en}} To grow [[#Adjective|plump]]; to [[swell out]].
#: ''Her cheeks have '''plumped'''.''
# {{context|intransitive|lang=en}} To [[drop]] or [[fall]] suddenly or heavily, all at once.
#* ''Spectator''
#*: Dulcissa '''plumps''' into a chair.
# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To make plump; to fill (out) or support; often with ''up''.
#* Fuller
#*: to '''plump''' up the hollowness of their history with improbable miracles
# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To [[cast]] or let drop all at once, suddenly and heavily.
#: ''to '''plump''' a stone into water''
# {{context|intransitive|lang=en}} To give a [[plumper]] (kind of vote).
# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To give (a vote), as a plumper.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er|more}}

# Having a full and rounded shape; [[chubby]], [[somewhat]] [[overweight]].
#: {{ux|en|a '''plump''' baby;&emsp; '''plump''' cheeks}}
#* {{w|Thomas Carew}} (1595-1640)
#*: The god of wine did his '''plump''' clusters bring.
#* {{quote-book|year=1956|author={{w|Delano Ames}}|chapter=23|title=[http://openlibrary.org/works/OL5915292W Crime out of Mind]|passage=He was a '''plump''' little man and we had been walking uphill at a pace—set by him—far too rapid for his short legs.  He breathed stertorously, and half the drops which glimmered on his rotund face were not rain but sweat.}}
# [[fat|Fat]].

